      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Betablockers reduce mortality by 30% after a myocardial infarction. The anti anginal effects of betablockers are also very well established. They improve survival after a non cardiac surgery in patients at high cardiovascular risk. Atenolol should nevertheless be avoided for primary cardiovascular protection in patients with hypertension older than 55 yrs. This may not apply to more selective betablockers, or betablockers with vasodilator effects. We also now have another bradycardic agent, ivabradine, which may prove very useful in heart failure patients who cannot tolerate a betablocker."},
